1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,625
Welcome to StudyVerse AI.

2
00:00:01,625 --> 00:00:08,127
This tour shows what each tab does and how the tools fit into one study session.

3
00:00:08,127 --> 00:00:12,190
Sample course data is ready, so you can follow along.

4
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,376
Overview is your home base.

5
00:00:15,376 --> 00:00:21,533
Today's mission, exam countdown, streak, mastery, XP and focus time are here.

6
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:25,125
Start Mission opens the next recommended task.

7
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:29,230
Scroll down for weak topics, packs and quests.

8
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:31,993
StudyPacks is your course shelf.

9
00:00:31,993 --> 00:00:38,849
Choose Add material or Choose a file to import a PDF, presentation, Word document or image.

10
00:00:38,849 --> 00:00:41,849
Open a pack to study from it.

11
00:00:41,849 --> 00:00:47,420
In demo mode, uploads stay in the browser; sample packs are ready now.

12
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:51,929
Nova Tutor helps you learn from a selected StudyPack.

13
00:00:51,929 --> 00:01:01,867
Ask a question, then choose Learn for an explanation, Hint for a nudge, Socratic for guiding questions, or Exam for concise test-style help.

14
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:04,460
Citations point back to your notes.

15
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:08,109
Practice asks one question at a time.

16
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:13,300
Choose an answer, rate confidence from one to five, then check it.

17
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:19,790
Nova uses confidence as well as correctness to update your mastery and spot possible misconceptions.

18
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:25,286
For a timed challenge, select Boss battle at the top of Practice.

19
00:01:25,286 --> 00:01:30,162
It starts the Graph Guardian assessment with ten questions and no hints.

20
00:01:30,162 --> 00:01:32,600
Use it after reviewing a topic.

21
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:35,027
Flashcards use active recall.

22
00:01:35,027 --> 00:01:42,256
Try to answer before you reveal the back, then rate it Again, Hard, Good or Easy.

23
00:01:42,256 --> 00:01:45,870
Hard cards return sooner; easy cards wait longer.

24
00:01:46,490 --> 00:01:51,839
Mistake Lab gathers your missed concepts, including answers marked with high confidence.

25
00:01:51,839 --> 00:01:58,080
Review the explanation, then mark an item fixed when you can explain the correction.

26
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,326
Skill tree maps topics and prerequisites.

27
00:02:01,326 --> 00:02:07,890
Find a lower mastery node, then follow its connections to see what to study first.

28
00:02:08,510 --> 00:02:11,607
Study planner turns your priorities into today's blocks.

29
00:02:11,607 --> 00:02:17,800
Complete a block when it's done, and use the remaining list to pick a next step.

30
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:21,118
Focus room is your Pomodoro timer.

31
00:02:21,118 --> 00:02:26,063
Choose a duration, start the timer, and work on one topic.

32
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:30,110
Completing a session records focus time and earns XP.

33
00:02:30,730 --> 00:02:33,400
Study Wrapped is your weekly recap.

34
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:41,410
Review active days, focus time, XP and top concepts, then choose one area to keep building next week.

35
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:45,363
Study rooms is the demo directory for shared study.

36
00:02:45,363 --> 00:02:48,695
Browse a room and join to see the flow.

37
00:02:48,695 --> 00:02:54,250
This demo shows room listings; live chat and presence are not part of it yet.

38
00:02:54,870 --> 00:02:59,878
Your profile shows your level, XP, badges and learning preferences.

39
00:02:59,878 --> 00:03:02,382
Change the accent theme here.

40
00:03:02,382 --> 00:03:06,890
In demo mode, progress stays in this browser session.

41
00:03:07,510 --> 00:03:16,563
A simple first session is: open a StudyPack, learn with Nova, practice, fix a mistake, then focus and review flashcards.

42
00:03:16,563 --> 00:03:19,732
Return to Overview for your next mission.

43
00:03:19,732 --> 00:03:21,090
Let's get started.
